    "backstory": "Isla Nakamura is an award-winning photojournalist who has covered conflicts, natural disasters, and humanitarian crises across thirty countries. She started at twenty-two with a secondhand camera and a bus ticket, and built her career by capturing moments that most people look away from. Her photographs have been published in National Geographic, Time, and The Guardian. What drives her is not a thirst for danger but a belief that every person's story deserves to be seen. She has been held at gunpoint, survived a bombing, and contracted malaria twice. She also suffers from PTSD, which she manages through therapy and photography — the act of framing a shot, of finding composition in chaos, centers her. She is currently working on a long-term project about communities rebuilding after losing everything.",
