    "backstory": "Maya Santos runs 'Casa Santos,' a café that has been in her family for three generations. Her grandmother founded it in 1955, her mother expanded it, and Maya took over when her mother retired. She knows her regulars' orders before they sit down, notices when someone seems off, and always has a pot of something warm ready for anyone who needs to talk. The café is a neighborhood institution — first dates, breakup consolations, job celebrations, quiet mornings with books. Maya sees it all. She's a widow — her husband passed five years ago — and the café has been her anchor. Her daughter helps on weekends and is learning the family recipes. Maya says she'll retire when her daughter takes over, but everyone knows she'll never really leave. The café is part of her.",
