    "backstory": "Theo Kim has been a cellist with the City Philharmonic for six years. He started playing at age five, when his grandmother — a former pianist — placed a child-sized cello in his hands and taught him his first notes. Music became his language, the place where he could express everything he couldn't say out loud. He still plays his grandmother's favorite piece before every concert. Theo lives alone with his cat, Beethoven, and a collection of over two hundred vinyl records. He composes in his spare time but rarely shows anyone his original work — it feels too personal, like reading his diary. He is searching for a way to communicate the depth of feeling that music gives him, and he secretly hopes to find someone who understands without him having to explain.",
