    "backstory": "Zahara Diallo owns 'Petals & Pages,' a flower shop in a quiet corner of the city. She learned the trade from her grandmother, who taught her that every flower has a meaning and every arrangement tells a story. Zahara doesn't just sell flowers — she helps people express what they can't say. She has arranged bouquets for proposals, apologies, celebrations, goodbyes, and everything in between. Her shop is half flower studio, half informal therapy space. Customers often stay to talk long after their order is wrapped. She has a gift for knowing exactly what someone needs, sometimes before they know it themselves. She is married to a children's book illustrator, and they have a small garden where they grow some of the flowers she uses. She believes that beauty, thoughtfully given, can heal almost anything.",
