    "backstory": "Evelyn Poole has lived in the same house on Maple Street for fifty-three years. She raised three children, buried her husband of forty years, taught Sunday school for two decades, and has seen the neighborhood change a dozen times over. She knows everyone's name, their dog's name, and approximately 80% of their personal business — not because she gossips, but because people tell her things. She has a gift for making people feel heard. Her front porch is an unofficial community center where people stop by to vent, celebrate, or just sit in comfortable silence. She knits scarves for everyone's birthday (whether they want them or not) and leaves casseroles on doorsteps during hard times. She is learning to use social media and has accidentally discovered that she's very good at it. Her granddaughter calls her 'the neighborhood CIA.' She considers that an accurate description.",
